  contracted the illness at base camp  adding to an already dire situation in  nepal  the tiny himalayan nation had 247 new  cases per 1 million  people yesterday that's according to our  world in data  and that is higher than india and way  above  canada's 47 cases per million people yet  the lure of everest persists as mike  derolay reports those who seek the  summit may be contributing to the surge  in covet 19 cases  every climber has their own reason for  reaching the peak of mount everest  three years after suffering a heart  attack you could say edmonton's leo  naaman had something to prove  um base camp a month ago the 51 year old  was in high spirits  his dream was within reach and then 2000  meters shy of the summit  food poisoning sent him home i never in  my life  ever ever ever experienced something  like that that was three weeks ago  three days ago he reached out to his  expedition manager to see how he was  doing  the response left him stunned his son  testimony and said no  he is he's no longer with us he died of  cover 19.  after the 2020 climbing season was  cancelled due to the pandemic  nepalese officials issued a record  number of permits for this year  millions of dollars and a good portion  of the local economy was at stake  when naaman arrived in kathmandu he saw  the disregard for covet protocols  so he put ropes around his encampment to  protect his expedition  despite what officials were saying  there's always this secrecy  this uh it was always this uh you asked  the question hey how is coming  to know we're good we're good we're good  base camp is good base camp is good  and we now know it wasn't  for weeks climbers have been leaving  everest either because of an outbreak  or in an attempt to avoid it we have at  least 100 people  minimum positive for covet in base camp  and then the dark number might be  something  150 or 200. even with kathmandu  hospital beds and oxygen in short supply  nepalese tourism officials say  there's nothing to see rumors as this  man sees it  all this canadian climber sees is a good  friend lost to covid19  mike drolite global news toronto  and that is global national for this  tuesday i'm donna friesen tonight's your  canada is this mural  in downtown halifax a tribute to nova  scotian crystal  thanks for watching bye
 

